# E11 read-to-learn: exact queue commands (printed by `python -m vsa_embed.experiments.e11_read_to_learn plan --include-pending`).
# NOT EXECUTED by the agent that wrote them. Run from the repository root of the main checkout after merging this branch:
#   cd /home/bhux/workplace/VSA-LLM && PY=/home/bhux/anaconda3/envs/vsa-repro/bin/python
# Priorities: 62 = gradient lr choice on the dev words (must run first); 63 = tier 1 (primary endpoints: T5-N 360M C5/C0′
# seeds 1–3, T4-H 360M C5/C0′); 64 = tier 2 (replications, controls, T5-H 360M, T4-N 360M, T1-H, 135M T5-N/T4-H);
# 65 = tier 3 (T5-H / T4-N on 135M); 66 = pooled report. Lower numbers run first; the queue holds pending jobs at 51–61.
# Jobs marked "after T4 seeds 2–3 train" (names with -s2 / -s3 under e11-t4-*) need those E9 runs' final.pt first:
# queue them only once experiments/e9-retrofit/runs/t4/<host>-full-<model>-s{2,3}/final.pt exist.
# GPU-h figures are idle-GPU estimates from the smoke test (preregistration §12). Optional, not queued here: the Claude
# teacher reader (`e11_read_to_learn teacher --items DIR`, ≈ $25–45 over all open-licence sets; author decision).
set -euo pipefail
: "${PY:?set PY to the pinned interpreter}"

